From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:07:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(providers): per-account login dir on subscription
 providers

Carried on custom while the design is discussed on upstream issue #503;
see docs/providers.md. Drop it once upstream has an equivalent.

A subscription provider always used the CLI's single login (~/.claude or
~/.codex), so a host could not hold two Claude Max accounts, or two
ChatGPT accounts, side by side.

A claude/codex subscription entry now accepts config_dir, the login
directory of that account. It is exported as CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR for Claude
and as the source CODEX_HOME for Codex:

- SDK harnesses get it in the spawn env from the resolved provider.
- Hosts export the default account's directory into every runner they
  launch, and `omnigent claude` / `omnigent codex` apply it at startup,
  so native CLIs and the files Omnigent reads for them agree.
- A spec that pins an account whose directory differs from the one the
  native CLI runs with fails instead of running on the wrong login.
- Readiness checks read the default account's own login, and a Codex
  account with its own directory never falls back to another credential.
- `omnigent setup` can add another account for a CLI that already has a
  subscription, signing it into its own directory; removing one signs out
  of that directory only.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Docs: none (documented with its series in docs/providers.md)
